<div class="eyebrow">AJSMR POLICY</div><h1>Data Availability &amp; Research Data Policy</h1><section><h2>Purpose</h2><p>AJSMR encourages transparent and responsible sharing of research data so that published findings can be understood, verified and, where appropriate, reproduced.</p></section><section><h2>Data Availability Statement</h2><p>Authors should provide a clear statement describing where supporting data can be accessed, whether data are available on reasonable request, or why restrictions apply.</p></section><section><h2>Repositories</h2><p>Where suitable, authors are encouraged to deposit supporting datasets in an appropriate recognized repository and provide a persistent identifier or link.</p></section><section><h2>Sensitive Data</h2><p>Human participant, confidential, proprietary or otherwise restricted data must not be shared in a manner that violates consent, privacy, law or contractual obligations.</p></section><section><h2>Data Integrity</h2><p>Authors remain responsible for the accuracy, completeness and appropriate documentation of the data underlying their article.</p></section>
